{"id": "unknown-2026-09-08-006", "date": "2026-09-08", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "South Korea to expand renewable monitoring mandate to 20 kW", "content": "<p>The South Korean government says it will require far smaller solar, wind and fuel-cell installations to carry real-time monitoring and remote-control capability from 2027, easing the switch to commercial mobile networks along the way.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/08/south-korea-to-expand-renewable-monitoring-mandate-to-20-kw/\">South Korea to expand renewable monitoring mandate to 20 kW</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Glob", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/08/south-korea-to-expand-renewable-monitoring-mandate-to-20-kw/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-08-007", "date": "2026-09-08", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.75, "keywords": ["dominant", "expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "HiNa Battery scales Korean sodium-ion partnership from 15 MWh to 10 GWh", "content": "<p>HiNa Battery signed a five-year deal to supply South Korea’s Volta with 10 GWh of sodium-ion batteries, expanding an earlier 15 MWh storage partnership. The agreement highlights sodium-ion technology’s shift toward GWh-scale energy storage deployments, though LFP batteries remain dominant in the market.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/08/hina-battery-scales-korean-sodium-ion-partnership-from-15-mwh-to-10-gwh/\">HiNa Battery scales Korean sodium-ion partnership from", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/08/hina-battery-scales-korean-sodium-ion-partnership-from-15-mwh-to-10-gwh/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-08-008", "date": "2026-09-08", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "North Macedonia’s BESS market begins to develop", "content": "<p>Analysis from Solar Macedonia says both standalone and co-located battery projects are beginning to materialise, while recent drought conditions have been favorable to the economic viability of solar projects.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/08/north-macedonias-bess-market-begins-to-develop/\">North Macedonia’s BESS market begins to develop</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/08/north-macedonias-bess-market-begins-to-develop/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-08-009", "date": "2026-09-08", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "‘It looks like there could be an undersupply of the highest efficiency’", "content": "<p>Alastair Mounsey, VP for Europe discusses JA's solar moduel module strategy, why quality matters, and the growing role of energy storage in the business. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/08/it-looks-like-there-could-be-an-undersupply-of-the-highest-efficiency/\">&#8216;It looks like there could be an undersupply of the highest efficiency&#8217;</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/08/it-looks-like-there-could-be-an-undersupply-of-the-highest-efficiency/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-08-010", "date": "2026-09-08", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Yemen’s largest solar plant set to double to 240 MW", "content": "<p>Yemen is expanding its largest solar power plant in Aden from 120 MW to 240 MW with UAE funding, while plans for a separate 50 MW project in Hadhramaut are also advancing. The projects form part of a growing pipeline of utility-scale solar developments across the country.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/08/yemens-largest-solar-plant-set-to-double-to-240-mw/\">Yemen’s largest solar plant set to double to 240 MW</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/08/yemens-largest-solar-plant-set-to-double-to-240-mw/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-08-011", "date": "2026-09-08", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["trade_tariff", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Liberia renews suspension of import tariffs on off-grid solar products", "content": "<p>Liberia's suspension of import tariffs on off-grid solar products has been extended as the country looks to stimulate private investment and expand access to clean energy.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/08/liberia-renews-suspension-of-import-tariffs-on-off-grid-solar-products/\">Liberia renews suspension of import tariffs on off-grid solar products</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/08/liberia-renews-suspension-of-import-tariffs-on-off-grid-solar-products/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-08-012", "date": "2026-09-08", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Great Power successfully completes full-scale fire test", "content": "<p>Great Power has completed a full-scale fire test of its 5 MWh energy storage system, with no fire propagation to adjacent containers, no structural collapse, and no thermal runaway observed in any adjacent module.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/08/great-power-successfully-completes-full-scale-fire-test/\">Great Power successfully completes full-scale fire test</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/08/great-power-successfully-completes-full-scale-fire-test/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-08-013", "date": "2026-09-08", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Hoymiles releases bidirectional EV charger", "content": "<p>The V2X DC Charger has up to 22 kW of DC charging power. It features IP65 protection and IK10 impact protection. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/08/hoymiles-releases-bidirectional-ev-charger/\">Hoymiles releases bidirectional EV charger</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/08/hoymiles-releases-bidirectional-ev-charger/", "type": "rss"}]}
